 "text": "Hey there, how are you feeling? Snow is tough on tires. Are yours still in the middle of the tread, or getting close to the worn line? That usually means they' almost worn. A professional can give you an accurate reading, and you only paying for the time if they need swapping. Stick to the main roads, avoid stopping if you can, and drive slowly. Brake gently and avoid sudden acceleration or braking. A snow sock, a spare tyre, and the right tools for changing it on the road are the basics.",
